Title: BASEMENT TAPE
Author: Kevin Shaw
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. SUBURBAN HOUSE - BASEMENT - NIGHT

LEAH PARK, 30s, clears boxes after her father's funeral. A VHS CAMCORDER and a stack of tapes sit on a shelf.
LEAH
Last thing I need is home movies.

INT. BASEMENT - LATER

Curiosity wins. Leah plugs in the camcorder. A tape labeled CHRISTMAS '94 plays — family dinner, her father young, laughing.
The image glitches. The same dinner repeats. Her father stares into lens.
ON TAPE — FATHER
Leah, don't rewind this one.

INT. BASEMENT - NIGHT

Leah checks the tape label again. CHRISTMAS '94. The timestamp reads 3:07 AM.
LEAH
Dad, you died on a Tuesday. Not at three in the morning.

INT. BASEMENT STAIRS - NIGHT

The basement light flickers. Footsteps creak overhead — but Leah lives alone.
LEAH
Hello?

INT. BASEMENT - NIGHT

On the tiny screen, her father stands in this basement, pointing at the floor trapdoor Leah never noticed. The live trapdoor sits behind her, slightly open.
ON TAPE — FATHER
You were always down here. You just forgot.

FADE OUT.


THE END
